{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/371833-the-number-of-elder-dragon-blooded","id":371833,"title":"The number of Elder Dragon-Blooded?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-15T21:48:32-08:00","id":371833,"title":"The number of Elder Dragon-Blooded?","content":"Were we ever given an idea on how many Dragon-Blooded alive could qualify for Elder Essence levels? It seems that capturing them and using Three Fold Binding of the Heart on them is something that a lot of beings with Celestial Sorcery might be interested in. I imagine that most DBs, once they get some age, learn to be bad asses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T22:32:34-08:00","id":371903,"title":"","content":"There's probably quite a lot of monks with Essence 6 and a few other Elders (monks spend a lot more time meditating to achieve enlightenment than everyone else). Very few above Essence 6 though, simply due to age.<br /> <br /> Also, Threefold Binding of the Heart isn't that great on elder DBs, because IIRC, they have an Integrity charm that breaks mental influence on them. It costs 10m, 1wp and 1hl.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T22:42:41-08:00","id":371923,"title":"","content":"This is the sort of complex speculative math that gets really variable, really fast. First, we don't exactly have a good grasp on just how many dragon-blooded there even are. One in 10,000 people is a number handed out in places, but it is not clear what the population of Creation is going to be, especially since 3e makes the map a lot bigger and adds considerably more fertile temperate areas (and retcons big chunks of 'the north' back into the temperate zone). Personally I like the 700-800 million range, so that there's 1 celestial exalt for every million people. That yields 70,000-80,000 dragon-blooded (not sure how many Exigents/Getinmians/Liminals yet).<br /> <br /> If we split the difference and go with 75,000 dragon-blooded, then the question is how many are essence 6+, correct? That depends on how you calculate background XP, what proportion of dragon-blooded survive to the relevant age, and what proportion of dragon-blooded start with essence 3 instead of essence 2. Also it additionally depends on the confounding factors of 1. Sorcery and 2. Martial Arts Mastery. Both of those can prolong lifespan considerably, inducing an unusual feedback loop in that the most powerful dragon-blooded are those most likely to live the longest. Ragara Myrrun, if he doesn't explode, isn't staring down mortality for a very long time.<br /> <br /> Honestly, in a 2e context, the answer is 'enough to make the Deathlords think that immediate world conquest isn't happening even with Abyssals and no empress while also intimidating the Lunars that the same thing is true.' Given that, even if only one dragon-blooded in one hundred makes it to essence 6 that would give you quite literally thousands of them at that level and that that would probably supply the Realm and other powers with the necessary elders to hold back the celestial exalts, I think that's a defensible ratio.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1j0RQNTrhSQVIjBJw3555qA1S9Hih1SRwychiPhEwm9k/pub\" target=\"_blank\">Whitescrub Tundra Project</a>: a fan-made setting reference for Exalted 3e.<br /> <a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/10769032/1/\" target=\"_blank\">Edge of Underleaves</a> A pair of dragon-blooded dare the jungles of the southwest.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4060-mechalich","name":"Mechalich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4060_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"133"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T23:06:36-08:00","id":371969,"title":"","content":"Something like 1/4 to a 1/3 of Dynasts die before making new little Dynasts (mostly from punching above their weight-class while adventuring in sword brotherhoods, with calculated political inhumations filling the number out). So we can ignore them, since this will happen long before Essence 6 becomes a thing. You can probably figure that die-off climbs significantly higher for non-Dynasts, who have to contend with the same threats but less access to the beat-em-up toys of the Realm - though I would also assume Lookshy DBs fall much closer to Dynasts on that scale. Then you have to consider the realities of Realm politics. Raising essence needs a month per dot in meditation and seclusion past E3. This is not a situation that lends itself to maintaining your position in Realm politics, much less improving it (and Lookshy is probably just as cut-throat, if not as blatantly antagonistic). E3 to E4 is a good investment for your House or Gente, because it provides more power and Charm access. But E5 for mid-level schlubs is going to be expensive in terms of time off and effectively create another rival for House/Gente control. So, you average House/Gentes leader is going to work most underlings too hard to be able to increase Essence beyond 4, excepting groomed heirs and other favorites - and that would still be dependent upon not losing political power in the downtime cycle. The IF probably offers more chance for Essence advancement. Realistically, probably only 10% or so are going to ever hit E5. But, those 10% are going to also have the time and age to keep pushing, so I would figure most would hit E6 (though political realities probably push that off until closer to 200 years, rather than at 100 years).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1651-phalamir","name":"phalamir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T00:00:57-08:00","id":372021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/371833-the-number-of-elder-dragon-blooded?p=371923#post371923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the sort of complex speculative math that gets really variable, really fast. First, we don't exactly have a good grasp on just how many dragon-blooded there even are. One in 10,000 people is a number handed out in places, but it is not clear what the population of Creation is going to be, especially since 3e makes the map a lot bigger and adds considerably more fertile temperate areas (and retcons big chunks of 'the north' back into the temperate zone). Personally I like the 700-800 million range, so that there's 1 celestial exalt for every million people. That yields 70,000-80,000 dragon-blooded (not sure how many Exigents/Getinmians/Liminals yet).</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC, the books say there are 20,000 DBs. 10,000 (approximately) in the Realm, and 10,000 (approximately) outside it: Lookshy, random outcastes, local ruling dyasties, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If we split the difference and go with 75,000 dragon-blooded, then the question is how many are essence 6+, correct? That depends on how you calculate background XP, what proportion of dragon-blooded survive to the relevant age, and what proportion of dragon-blooded start with essence 3 instead of essence 2. Also it additionally depends on the confounding factors of 1. Sorcery and 2. Martial Arts Mastery. Both of those can prolong lifespan considerably, inducing an unusual feedback loop in that the most powerful dragon-blooded are those most likely to live the longest. Ragara Myrrun, if he doesn't explode, isn't staring down mortality for a very long time. </div> </div> </div>All Dragon-blood (well, all Exalts) start with Essence 2. Some have spent their time before you might actually play them, raising their essence, while others have spent it training their abilities or attributes. But if you played a game where you were all 14 year olds who literally exalted yesterday, you'd have Essence 2 (and less abilities, attributes and charms than the character gen rules: those are for people who've finished their schooling, so have probably been exalted for years already).<br /> Secondly, neither Martial Arts or Sorcery prolong your lifespan. The things that prolong your lifespan are: money (for anagathics), resistance (ie being healthy), and that charm for extending your lifespan (it's either Resistance 6 or Medicine 6, I forget). And not doing anything dangerous (like, say, constant kung fu duels, or messing around with demons... but saying that, both of those are safer than being a soldier).<br /> They are, however, things that encourage you to take the time to meditate and raise your essence, whereas if you're a bureaucrat it's really not all that important.<br /> <br /> Ballpark figure, I'd say there are 200 DBs with Essence 6 in the Realm (1 out of 50 DBs), and 75% of them are Monks (and therefore, actually very good at personal combat).<br /> <br /> I should say, however, having played high-essence DBs, I don't think there's a colossal difference between Essence 5 and Essence 6. The power level doesn't increase exponentially. At essence 5, if you're a master of war, you can already nuke battlefields, and you need to be Essence 7 to be better at it. When I was playing a very, very, long-running game, we got over 1000xp, we were all Essence 5, and I (and a few of the others I think) wished I could get to Essence 6. I wasn't thinking &quot;wow, my charms will be massively super-powerful compared to what I have now if I was Essence 6!&quot;, I was thinking &quot;I have every attribute and ability I care about at 5, I wish I could buy the ones my character should be best at to 6. so I can differentiate his specialities again&quot;.<br /> <br /> If I was a Deathlord, sure the small number of Essence 6 DBs is scary, but I'm far, far more worried about the thousand or so Essence 4 DBs, because they will make mincemeat out of my 5 Abyssals who've only been Exalted for 5 years.<br /> <br /> (I should also say, fighting a 150 year old DB is scary, but it's less because he might be Essence 6 and more the fact that he has tons of charms and quite possibly spells and celestial-tier martial arts, not to mention more artefacts than your average Solar circle)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T00:11:59-08:00","id":372059,"title":"","content":"I generally run with the idea that there are between 200-300 DBs in the Realm with Essence 6+, and about half that number outside of the Realm. These guys tend to be very old, very experienced, very wealthy and many of them have pretty large families.<br /> <br /> Then there's maybe a two dozen DB's in Creation with an Essence of 7 and even that is probably a generous estimate, and those guys are pretty much the biggest badasses you will ever meet in Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T01:51:56-08:00","id":372120,"title":"","content":"Those seem like pretty reasonable numbers to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T02:46:49-08:00","id":372149,"title":"","content":"The fact that there would logically be so many Dragon Blooded over the fairly generous age of 100 seems to me to be a point on why tying Essence potential to age, especially relatively young ages, was not really a good idea. I would not be averse to saying that in the entire history of the Realm, there have been maybe a few dozen Dragon Blooded with greater than Essence 5. Dynasts generally have more immediate pressing concerns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T04:29:08-08:00","id":372203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/371833-the-number-of-elder-dragon-blooded?p=372149#post372149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that there would logically be so many Dragon Blooded over the fairly generous age of 100 seems to me to be a point on why tying Essence potential to age, especially relatively young ages, was not really a good idea..</div> </div> </div> </div>Except it is a minimum. If you want to be the Immaculate monk who sits on a rock diddling his chakras 24/7, then I see no reason to stop you. But a secular Dynast doing the same is going to be so underdeveloped in virtually every area that is meaningful. 'I have bigger mote pool&quot; doesn't really mean jack compared to &quot;I have the skills, aptitudes, Charms, and social standing to put your enlightened ass deep in the cold ground - and then blame it all on my enemies&quot;. It really is a self-correcting problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1651-phalamir","name":"phalamir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T14:49:53-08:00","id":372912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Secondly, neither Martial Arts or Sorcery prolong your lifespan. </div> </div> </div>The books explicitly mention that both martial arts and sorcery can prolong your lifespan above and beyond the more mundane methods. Examples are given in the case of martial artists, notably the Masters of Even Blade Style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1j0RQNTrhSQVIjBJw3555qA1S9Hih1SRwychiPhEwm9k/pub\" target=\"_blank\">Whitescrub Tundra Project</a>: a fan-made setting reference for Exalted 3e.<br /> <a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/10769032/1/\" target=\"_blank\">Edge of Underleaves</a> A pair of dragon-blooded dare the jungles of the southwest.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4060-mechalich","name":"Mechalich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4060_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"133"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T17:08:18-08:00","id":373091,"title":"","content":"Immediate world conquest isn't happening for the Deathlords because the world is pretty huge, it's full of a diverse array of strange and powerful things, and only a few of them are especially motivated for it. I think the real question should be &quot;depending on what one decides the actual premise of elder Dragon Blooded power are, does it benefit the portrayal of the Realm to picture there as being lots of them?&quot; Personally, I don't think the Realm benefited from the idea that it should be portrayed as though it had even a single Terrestrial capable of As In the Beginning, let alone several hundred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T18:07:15-08:00","id":373143,"title":"","content":"I'd be happy for 1 guy to be able to do it: Ragara, the oldest Dragonblood. Of course, he's so old that's doddering and frail and has no idea what's going on. So that maybe you could do a plot hook where the PCs have to wheel out the senile Ragara and point him at the enemy. Or perhaps try to steal a peach of immortality to make him young again so he can save the day.<br /> On the other hand, Ragara's always portrayed as a massive chump, so maybe that's too good a power for him.<br /> <br /> But I do prefer the Realm to conquer things with their armies than by nuking everything. That's what they have the Sword of Creation for (which comes with significant drawbacks).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The books explicitly mention that both martial arts and sorcery can prolong your lifespan above and beyond the more mundane methods. Examples are given in the case of martial artists, notably the Masters of Even Blade Style. </div> </div> </div>Really? Because there's no rules anywhere for doing it that way, and I don't see anything about that in the description of that style. It says they made the style 200 years ago, but since DBs live for like 300 years before anagathics, that's not strange.<br /> Of course, practicing martial arts is a good form of exercise that helps old people keep limber: I see a ton of old people doing tai chi every morning near my apartment. It's kind of funny when you walk to work past three or four 80 year old grandmothers waving sabres around to tinny Mao-era music. So it might add 2 or 3 years to your life. But I assume you meant a significant increase.<br /> (Admittedly, they do say in the fluff that both the Empress and Mnemon use sorcery to keep themselves young, but no spell for doing this was every published, and when Mnemon was statted up they just gave her a gem of immortality. I actually think that a spell for making you live longer would be pretty in-theme, but none have ever been shown,)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T18:18:20-08:00","id":373150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/371833-the-number-of-elder-dragon-blooded?p=373143#post373143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be happy for 1 guy to be able to do it: Ragara, the oldest Dragonblood.</div> </div> </div> </div>The oldest <i>living</i> Dragon-Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T18:32:26-08:00","id":373182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because there's no rules anywhere for doing it that way</div> </div> </div> </div> I could have sworn you were on our side of this camp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T18:47:49-08:00","id":373208,"title":"","content":"Even going strictly by the rules of age limits, Well Tended Garden Of The Soul is available at Essence 5 and can extend a Dragon-Blood's life indefinitely. <br /> <br /> It seems a glib answer, but there should be as many elder Essence Dragon-Bloods as are appropriate for your game. If you need dozens or hundreds of elder Dragon-Bloods for the Realm to be a credible threat in your story, you should do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T19:04:37-08:00","id":373214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/371833-the-number-of-elder-dragon-blooded?p=373182#post373182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I could have sworn you were on our side of this camp.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha, that made me laugh. You're right, I do prefer going by the fluff to the mechanics, and if they'd written &quot;martial arts and sorcery extend your life a ton&quot; all over the place, I'd say they do, and damn the lack of rules. I'm not opposed to that.<br /> I just haven't seen it anywhere except with the Empress and Mnemon (who as I said, ended up with a hearthstone, indicating that perhaps the sorcery was metaphorical).<br /> Also, in terms of why Dragonblood in the Realm learn sorcery or martial arts, I've never got the impression they do it for a long life, which you'd think would be a fairly attractive reason.<br /> (Though, of course, when you're young, you rarely make decisions for your life by how they'll affect your total lifespan.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even going strictly by the rules of age limits, Well Tended Garden Of The Soul is available at Essence 5 and can extend a Dragon-Blood's life indefinitely. </div> </div> </div>That's the one I was thinking of, is it in Resistance or Medicine?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 01-16-2015, 10:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T19:09:47-08:00","id":373215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/371833-the-number-of-elder-dragon-blooded?p=373214#post373214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the one I was thinking of, is it in Resistance or Medicine?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually Survival. It's in DotFA. <br /> <br /> Initially it just adds dice to the once-a-decade Resistance roll to survive old age. At E6+ the Terrestrial can stunt his actions based on his harmonious connection with nature and his Dragon-Blooded heritage to prevent the difficulty of the roll from rising. Saibok Gauto demonstrates that it is possible for a Dragon-Blood to survive several thousand years in this fashion.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T19:23:17-08:00","id":373224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/371833-the-number-of-elder-dragon-blooded?p=373208#post373208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems a glib answer, but there should be as many elder Essence Dragon-Bloods as are appropriate for your game. If you need dozens or hundreds of elder Dragon-Bloods for the Realm to be a credible threat in your story, you should do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>In general, though, it's important for the game to avoid sending the message that you do need that. The Realm's power should be in its overarching structures (including <i>all</i> its DBs), not in a handful of superpowerful elder bombs.<br /> <br /> In 2e, when we discussed warfare and military strength in Exalted, things often came down to trying to figure out how many DBs there were capable of using <i>As In the Beginning</i>, because that was just a lot more important than boring stuff like armies or territory or supply routes. I think it's fair to say that 3e is not going back there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T19:24:04-08:00","id":373225,"title":"","content":"Wait, to everyone who says there are like a 100 Essence DBs in the whole Realm. Are talking about potentially E6 or that is the score that they have actually achieved? Because isn't 101 years old like early to mid 30s for a Dragon-Blooded?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T20:06:03-08:00","id":373247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/371833-the-number-of-elder-dragon-blooded?p=373225#post373225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, to everyone who says there are like a 100 Essence DBs in the whole Realm. Are talking about potentially E6 or that is the score that they have actually achieved? Because isn't 101 years old like early to mid 30s for a Dragon-Blooded?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually achieved. Raising Essence that high isn't a particularly good use of a Realm DB's time and effort (read XP), Few are going to have the requisite free time, much less the desire to do so at 101. The most likely candidates for E6 are going to be older DBs who have enough power to take 6 months off to stare at their navels and the political insulation to not get shafted during that time - or monks who have risen in position in the IF to have the freedom to meditate without also being stuck administering a monastery or temple. Most young-to-middle-age DBs have other problems to worry about. I built a century-old DB a few weeks ago for an NPC, She still had some specific Charm and ability holes I would have preferred to have extra XP to plug, and she was only Essence 4 . Racing to Essence 6 would have made her crappy at the job I designed her for. Rounding her out properly would probably take another 15-20 years of XP. And another 20-30 years over that would be nice to get her some fun extras. The handful of extra motes just isn't worth it, especially since the Charms she needs don't require anything beyond E4. Maybe around 150 years, she might consider raising her Essence to 5 for the top-level Charms, but E6 would still be put off until 175 at the earliest, and probably 200 as more realistic. It's just not that important to her life-track. As-is, she's a good field operative beginning to transition into the managerial side of things, where most 100 year old DBs are going to be","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1651-phalamir","name":"phalamir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T20:06:30-08:00","id":373249,"title":"","content":"Is there even still going to be a minimum age requirement for going up in essence to levels 6 and above? I don't recall them ever actually saying one way or another, just that it is generally not going to be worth the effort for an exalt to go higher then 5 anymore.<br /> <br /> But assuming the old 'must be 100+ to get essence 6' standard, I'd imagine that a lot of them are running around. But I'd imagine that the majority of dragon blooded with actual elder essence are immaculate monks, with a few exceptions like Mnemon who are perfectionists or whatever.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T20:22:00-08:00","id":373270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/371833-the-number-of-elder-dragon-blooded?p=373225#post373225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, to everyone who says there are like a 100 Essence DBs in the whole Realm. Are talking about potentially E6 or that is the score that they have actually achieved? Because isn't 101 years old like early to mid 30s for a Dragon-Blooded?</div> </div> </div> </div>Achieved.<br /> I think Phalamir's explanation above for why is pretty decent.<br /> <br /> Phalamir also raises a good point: in 2.5, when minimum damage isn't dependent on Essence, raising your essence, which is very expensive for DBs, gets you a total of 5 motes, and access to a few charms. But even with DotFA, there's only about 7 or 8 Essence 5 charms. So it's generally not really worth raising your essence from 4 to 5, compared to getting 4 more charms.<br /> Raising your essence is harder for Dragonblood than for anyone else, and they get less out of it.<br /> So the main people who are going to do it are monks, for whom meditating on their essence has (they believe) spiritual benefits, making them more likely to merge with the Dragons after their death.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In 2e, when we discussed warfare and military strength in Exalted, things often came down to trying to figure out how many DBs there were capable of using <i>As In the Beginning</i>, because that was just a lot more important than boring stuff like armies or territory or supply routes. I think it's fair to say that 3e is not going back there. </div> </div> </div>I certainly hope so. I'd also like to see the charm before that go, the Essence 5 one for nuking battlefields. We had two DB generals in our 1000xp game, both of them had War 5 and Essence 5, but if we faced off against a non-DB-led army, the best thing for them to do would be to nuke it. When being a master of commanding troops means you no longer need to command troops, things aren't right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T02:55:08-08:00","id":373439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">if they'd written &quot;martial arts and sorcery extend your life a ton&quot; all over the place, I'd say they do, and damn the lack of rules</div> </div> </div> </div> It actually tends to be mentioned in any place focused on the Dragon Blooded that details their lifespans. The closest to hand for me is page 281 of Exalted: the Dragon Blooded. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saibok Gauto demonstrates that it is possible for a Dragon-Blood to survive several thousand years in this fashion.</div> </div> </div> </div> Nah, he's just an abberation","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T07:10:40-08:00","id":373447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/371833-the-number-of-elder-dragon-blooded?p=373439#post373439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, he's just an abberation</div> </div> </div> </div>I read him as an example of someone fulfilling the required stunts of the Charm really well. The fact that his picture is right there next to the Charm may have reinforced this perception.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/371833-the-number-of-elder-dragon-blooded?p=373224#post373224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, though, it's important for the game to avoid sending the message that you do need that. The Realm's power should be in its overarching structures (including <i>all</i> its DBs), not in a handful of superpowerful elder bombs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I agree, but I realize some people like playing with high Essence Solar-tier Exalts as a default and it can be difficult for the Realm to pose a threat individually or collectively without powerhouses of their own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/371833-the-number-of-elder-dragon-blooded?p=373224#post373224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 2e, when we discussed warfare and military strength in Exalted, things often came down to trying to figure out how many DBs there were capable of using <i>As In the Beginning</i>, because that was just a lot more important than boring stuff like armies or territory or supply routes. I think it's fair to say that 3e is not going back there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the importance of As In The Beginning is overstated. Yes, it is a monstrously powerful weapon, but practically speaking Dragon Vortex Attack is probably more dangerous. A 9L Trauma 5 environmental hazard projected over most of your army <i>now</i> is a bigger threat than 100L hitting it in an hour's time.<br /> <br /> Because everyone avoids the Mass Combat rules it is often missed that the Thousand Correct Action Charms constitute a very robust War suite indeed. When combined with motes-per-magnitude group enhancing Charms, even Solar generals have trouble against DB backed Legions, which is as it should be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 01-17-2015, 11:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T07:58:06-08:00","id":373484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/371833-the-number-of-elder-dragon-blooded?p=373439#post373439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It actually tends to be mentioned in any place focused on the Dragon Blooded that details their lifespans. The closest to hand for me is page 281 of Exalted: the Dragon Blooded. Nah, he's just an abberation</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it's just in 1st ed, I don't remember it anywhere in 2nd ed (except as I said, with Mnemon and the Empress.)<br /> <br /> I'm fine with Martial Arts extending their lifespan a bit: it is good for your health after all. But I don't really see why it should increase their lifespan dramatically.<br /> <br /> As to sorcery, I do think it's in-genre for that to work, though obviously it should require a great cost in magical materials/virgin blood or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T09:13:35-08:00","id":373518,"title":"","content":"The best yard stick for essence levels for Terrestrials we have is the Realm since we have the most numbers and fluff relating to it. So you have to figure out what the Realm essence level ratio would be, then chop it down a bit and apply it to the rest of Creation.<br /> <br /> The best measurement I have found is the student class sizes in the various secondary schools. This gives us a rough idea of how many students go into each discipline.<br /> <br /> The Spiral Academy has 240 students a year.<br /> The Cloister of Wisdom can have up to 125, but rarely has max class levels.<br /> The House of Bells is never specified<br /> The Heptagram only has 75 students at any given time with some of them being graduates who are working on projects.<br /> <br /> According to that data alone, it seems that the majority of Terrestrials are becoming &quot;cubical dragons&quot;, which when you think about it means that they really don't need to raise their essence above 2 to use most of the charms they would need as a paper pusher.<br /> <br /> The Heptagram students require essence 3 to graduate, but they get diminishing returns on going higher in essence score. According to MoEP: Dragon-Blooded one Terrestrial in ten knows a single spell in the Realm even if they never went to the Heptagram, learned additional spells or never considered themselves &quot;sorcerers&quot;. This becomes important in that we now know at least 1,0000 or so Terrestrials are essence 3 or higher.<br /> <br /> The Cloister of Wisdom also requires Essence 3 to graduate, but with their CMA styles there is a clear benefit to pushing essence higher.<br /> <br /> Finally you have the House of Bells, which doesn't require a given essence level to graduate, but mote pool size = life in combat.<br /> <br /> But here is the kicker that a lot of people forget about, the two schools which would in theory gain the most from increasing essence score, are also the ones that will have the highest casualty rates. So those students who in theory would go higher in essence never get the chance. This in turn skews the population/essence numbers further.<br /> <br /> Now with all that in mind, lets look at the Realm itself. According to that one census report there are about 10,000 Terrestrials in the Realm (all great houses and Lost Eggs accounted for). But here is the kicker, that census took place a few years before the defeat at the hands of the Bull of the North, before the fall of Thorns which had Realm Terrestrial Advisors present, as well several other canon incidents which depict Terrestrials getting wacked left and right.<br /> <br /> That means that all those experienced Terrestrials are dead and the numbers have been replenished with low essence, low experience Terrestrials. So the Realm numbers at this point are probably less than 10,000 to say the least. But for the sake of easy math lets call it 10,000 and then assume the numbers will be lower than the math suggests, which in turn means the math for the rest of Creation with be even lower.<br /> <br /> Over all I would be comfortable with the following math for the Realm:<br /> <br /> Essence 2 Realm Terrestrials: 5,300<br /> Essence 3 Realm Terrestrials: 3,200<br /> Essence 4 Realm Terrestrials: 1,000<br /> Essence 5 Realm Terrestrials: 485<br /> Essence 6 Realm Terrestrials: 15<br /> <br /> So to answer the OP, under the best possible conditions, you are looking at 15 terrestrials out of every 10,000 that is elder essence levels. Probably less than that off the Blessed Isle due to higher risks or just lack of knowledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":727,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","user":"Thoth","date":". 01-17-2015, 12:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T09:35:56-08:00","id":373553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/371833-the-number-of-elder-dragon-blooded?p=373439#post373439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, he's just an abberation</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually he is a Terrestrial with undiluted blood. He fought in the Primordial War, which was way before the mortal blood got into the mix. So most standard rules are iffy to say the least.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T11:08:17-08:00","id":373622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/371833-the-number-of-elder-dragon-blooded?p=373484#post373484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe it's just in 1st ed, I don't remember it anywhere in 2nd ed (except as I said, with Mnemon and the Empress.)</div> </div> </div> </div>In the second edition book, it was put in a part that people would actually read. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Look at the end of the overall summary of a Dynast's life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I don't really see why it should increase their lifespan dramatically.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say it's an intertwined thing; the magic of the Martial Arts themselves combined with the pure and refined lifestyles that Dragon Blooded martial artists are liable to maintain in order to better integrate their Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Actually he is a Terrestrial with undiluted blood. He fought in the Primordial War, which was way before the mortal blood got into the mix. So most standard rules are iffy to say the least.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> The book outright states that he's an abberation. Like, he's the Exalted version of Henrietta Lacks, right down to how they've been extracting samples from him for ages trying to figure out how he works. I think it might even be that longevity Charm is supposed to be something other Dragon Blooded figured out by observing him, although I'd have to reread his stats.<br /> <br /> (Also, the concept of undiluted Dragon Blooded is terrible)</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T11:44:03-08:00","id":373641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/371833-the-number-of-elder-dragon-blooded?p=373622#post373622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Also, the concept of undiluted Dragon Blooded is terrible)</div> </div> </div> </div>Not having it around would be kind of weird in concert with the general Dragon-Blooded themes and, indeed, the themes of the setting as a whole, though, wouldn't it?<br /> <br /> The Dragon-Bloods were explicitly designed to be able to make good their losses (and increase their numbers) via breeding. Their Exaltation is a much less numinous thing than that of the Celestials; it's still transcendent, they're the Princes of the Earth for a good reason, but they're still of the earth, which means they're a sort of bloody, messy, practical kind of Exaltation. Their power flows through their bloodlines. That's kind of the point, right?<br /> <br /> The setting materiel on the Dragon-Blooded really hammers home the idea that power through bloodline and family and breeding is important. Families of Dragon-Blooded arrange powerful marriages and try to avoid getting mortal blood in there because they need to breed more Dragon-Bloods who are more powerful. Dynastic marriage politics are really really big deals. So is the fact that the Dragon-Bloods slept with absolutely everyone (and probably every<i>thing</i>) back in the day which is why occasionally their genetic soup mixes together with some random guy in the back of beyond and they pop as a new Prince of the Earth.<br /> <br /> It also ties into the whole &quot;everything in the Second Age is <i>less</i> than what it used to be&quot; theme going on. Dragon-Blooded aren't the immaculately bred killing machines with perfect ability to always give birth to more immaculately bred killing machines anymore. Sometimes even a scion of powerful bloodlines is just... not gonna Exalt. That's great. You can spin wonderful stories out of that!<br /> <br /> If diluting their blood doesn't matter at all, then all that goes right out the window, which I think would make the setting way less interesting than it is. There should, in my opinion, be a whole gamut running from &quot;everyone in my entire family going all the way back to the founding of the Realm is Dragon-Blooded, if there's mortal blood in there anywhere you'll never find it, all my siblings exalted, all my parents and their siblings exalted, I exalted, all my kids exalted. We're awesome. Who the fuck are <i>you</i>, you poorly-bred worm?&quot; down to &quot;okay, sure, I'm the first Exalt in this family of patricians for over 100 years, but I've done well, I worked my ass off in school, I bet I can marry upwards. I'd <i>better</i> marry upwards, for the good of my family. Oh, gods, I hope my kids exalt. They <i>really need</i> to exalt&quot; to &quot;man, fuck you, The Realm, I got lucky and totally scored this sweet-ass exaltation through pure luck. Yeah, I suppose some of my ancestors were Dragon-Bloods, that's how it works, and thank you kindly for making me all badass, but I don't really care about this whole thing. I'm gonna go walk off and take over a petty kingdom and have me a harem.&quot; With all points in-between!<br /> <br /> Not having the idea that once there were undiluted Dragon-Bloods, but now there are not, I think takes a lot of interesting stuff away from them.<br /> <br /> I will agree, as all right-thinking people do, that Breeding as it was mechanically implemented in the past is total and complete bullshit. I'm open to the idea of &quot;there's a background you can buy representing how especially awesome your bloodline is, you are gonna get all kinds of neat social bonuses because of it and maybe sometimes Pasiap sends you some kind of weird vision&quot; but I think we all agree that &quot;there's a background that gives you a shit-ton more motes&quot; is a stupid idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T11:54:47-08:00","id":373646,"title":"","content":"Mortals will probably be able to have the Breeding Merit in the new Edition. Consider the implications of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T12:02:27-08:00","id":373652,"title":"","content":"Also any time you feel inclined to say, &quot;[Exalt type] was explicitly designed to\u2026&quot;, it's time to rethink your position.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T12:08:08-08:00","id":373656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/371833-the-number-of-elder-dragon-blooded?p=373646#post373646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mortals will probably be able to have the Breeding Merit in the new Edition. Consider the implications of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mortals could actually have that merit in second edition actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T12:19:24-08:00","id":373663,"title":"","content":"To be clear, it's possible to disengage the concept of Dragon Blooded maintaining their mutual lineages and Dragon Blooded never having children with mortals. The mortal children of Mnemon are probably a by far superior match with a well bred Dynast than some rube from the Threshold whose great-great-great grandparent caught an Exalt's eye.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T14:43:33-08:00","id":373802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/371833-the-number-of-elder-dragon-blooded?p=373652#post373652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also any time you feel inclined to say, &quot;[Exalt type] was explicitly designed to\u2026&quot;, it's time to rethink your position.</div> </div> </div> </div>??<br /> <br /> &quot;The Solars were explicitly designed to be the champions of the Unconquered Sun.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The Abyssals were explicitly designed to destroy Creation.&quot;<br /> <br /> Those seem like factual, uncontroversial statements. I don't know why I would need to rethink stating them. The Exalt types are made things. There were both in-universe and out-of-universe reasons for how each Exalt type was designed, and some of those reasons are implicit and some of those reasons are explicit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/371833-the-number-of-elder-dragon-blooded?p=373663#post373663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be clear, it's possible to disengage the concept of Dragon Blooded maintaining their mutual lineages and Dragon Blooded never having children with mortals. The mortal children of Mnemon are probably a by far superior match with a well bred Dynast than some rube from the Threshold whose great-great-great grandparent caught an Exalt's eye.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything in those two sentences are absolutely true, but I don't see how they support the position that undiluted Dragon-Blooded are a bad idea. Indeed, both those sentences can only be true if the concept of &quot;Dragon-Bloods getting too much unExalted blood into their ancestry dilutes the chances of making more Dragon-Blooded and makes the ones who you do get less powerful&quot; is something that's completely true in-setting. Without that being a thing, it doesn't really matter who Mnemon's kids marry, does it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T17:11:56-08:00","id":373930,"title":"","content":"Yes, my prior statement suffers from a lack of specificity. I was focused on the concept as stated by Thoth and established in certain books of a concept of an original and superior form of Terrestrial Exalted that was only unsullied by congress with mortals. I <i>will</i> repeat my prior assertion that, before the Great Contagion, &quot;purity&quot; of bloodlines was often less of a concern. It is possible for the Dragon Blooded to exist in a context where they do not actually view having the best matches to produce the highest number of Exalted children possible as a high priority; contexts which might include relative prosperity and diversity of territories, or needing to avoid numbers that become so large that a measure of secrecy or flexibility becomes less viable.<br /> <br /> Indeed, my picture of the First Age (and Shogunate, to a lesser extent) is one in which the heredity of Terrestrial Exaltation was one that many individuals or small families used as a selling point for politically advantageous marriages to regionally powerful mortals; sometimes having the most Exalted children possible was less valuable than having Exalted children who would legitimise and entrench your position in a certain group.<br /> <br /> And really, even the actual Realm does not support unmitigated growth of the Dragon Blooded population. I would seriously doubt that there has ever been a point in the history of the Terrestrial Exalted where the heredity of their power was viewed as having the value of letting their numbers grow without limit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 01-18-2015, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T17:37:39-08:00","id":373934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/371833-the-number-of-elder-dragon-blooded?p=373930#post373930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, my prior statement suffers from a lack of specificity. I was focused on the concept as stated by Thoth and established in certain books of a concept of an original and superior form of Terrestrial Exalted that was only unsullied by congress with mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Without that concept, though, doesn't the whole breeding thing break down? If there was never a time when the Dragon-Blooded existed in a sort of idealized form, where they always bred true because they only bred with each other, then the whole bloodline thing breaks down.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is possible for the Dragon Blooded to exist in a context where they do not actually view having the best matches to produce the highest number of Exalted children possible as a high priority; contexts which might include relative prosperity and diversity of territories, or needing to avoid numbers that become so large that a measure of secrecy or flexibility becomes less viable. </div> </div> </div>In the Second Age, I don't think it is, because the Second Age is chronically short of Dragon-Blooded and always has been. It would only be possible for that context to exist if there are already &quot;enough&quot; Dragon-Blooded such that whenever whatever powers that be need one, one is always around.<br /> <br /> It's certainly possible to establish that context, but why would you want to? If you remove the incentive to produce good matches from the Dragon-Blooded as a society, you cut out a lot of potential plotlines, conflict, and drama.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Indeed, my picture of the First Age (and Shogunate, to a lesser extent) is one in which the heredity of Terrestrial Exaltation was one that many individuals or small families used as a selling point for politically advantageous marriages to regionally powerful mortals; sometimes having the most Exalted children possible was less valuable than having Exalted children who would legitimise and entrench your position in a certain group. </div> </div> </div>Hell, that's not even confined to the First Age. That's a thing in the modern Realm. The Great Houses are in a socially dominant position over the patrician class but the patrician class isn't without power and influence, and I believe it's been established that sometimes an Exalt will marry a well-bred patrician because of political or economic necessity. And the whole &quot;but what about the bloodline?&quot; thing makes that more interesting, rather than less, I think, because it's a countervailing incentive that has to be considered. You always want more Exalts, because that translates into more political and military power, especially in the long term, but in the here and now you really need that clan of powerful patrician merchants to align themselves with your Great House and not another one. What incentive wins out? And maybe the people whose lives you're playing Dynasty Chess with have their own opinions too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And really, even the actual Realm does not support unmitigated growth of the Dragon Blooded population. I would seriously doubt that there has ever been a point in the history of the Terrestrial Exalted where the heredity of their power was viewed as having the value of letting their numbers grow without limit. </div> </div> </div>On this one I'm going to have to disagree with you. The Realm seems like it has always been short of the numbers of Dragon-Blooded it would really like to have on hand. (Although maybe it was implied somewhere that the Empress values stability over expansion, so maybe she personally has a soft cap she'd prefer them not to surpass because then she'd have to conquer more of the world? I forget if that was a thing or not.) In fact, I've always gotten the impression that the Shogunate was as well, because the Shogunate was trying to hold together a global hegemony built on Solar infrastructure with only Dragon-Blooded, and the result of that was lots of Dragon-Blooded dying as they tried to hold back the Wyld and there were never enough Sorcerer-Technicians to go around and the like.<br /> <br /> You'd likely have to go all the way back to the Old Realm to get a context in which people are like &quot;yeah, we got plenty of Dragon-Blooded, and they tend to marry each other anyhow, and even when they don't their mortal lovers tend to produce Dragon-Blooded anyway, so purity of breeding isn't a big deal.&quot; And even in that context, you probably had Twilight's deciding things like &quot;no, you know what? This whole 'Exaltation through the blood' thing is interesting to me. How pure a Dragon-Blood can I develop?&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T17:53:57-08:00","id":373943,"title":"","content":"I always think that attaching Essence to age is a fundamental fault in most people's minds.<br /> <br /> Essence isn't something that just grows as you go, but a measure of enlightenment, of prowess in a very real sense. Essence 6 is kept away from Player Characters to mantain the theme of ancient, incredibly powerful old masters, but that doesn't mean that getting wrinkles on your face equals Essence. You can have Essence 5 15-year-olds (your Okita Soujis), and Essence 3 200-year-olds (your everyone else's).<br /> <br /> Attempting to tie it to demographics feels even weirder; 'My calculations tell me that we should have 10 Da Vincis and 15 Michelangelos currently!', and then you wonder why we don't have more Cistine Chapels.<br /> <br /> That gets even more strange when you consider Essence is not really a measure of <i>actual ability</i> in Exalted, and has never been: saying 'an Essence 6 character' accomplishes absolutely nothing. It is the array of Charms and Artifacts and connections that makes a character be actually relevant, and the amount of these entirely depends on how many named, important, earth-shaking characters you can have in mind. That <i>will vary between generations</i>. It absolutely has to! It's just how humans work! Those from generations that just happened to create several gifted figures will look upon a new generation with a certain contempt (even if some are gifted in different ways), and vice-versa, as older characters behold in a new generation so many children with talent such as he had never seen.<br /> <br /> Your game can have the 'Ten Bells', each an accomplished graduate of the House of Bells, once a Sworn Brotherhood, now sworn enemies, each of them a swordsman who has felled Anathema one-on-one; it can also have the Ledaal Council, comprised all of strange, eerie sages, some of which are more air than man, some of which have demonic shadows, some of which have become one with the stars, as her soul is entwined to a Sidereal lover's. And so on.<br /> <br /> Conversely, it's entirely possible that other than the examples we have sheets of, the only other Dragon-Blooded in the Realm with Essence higher than 4 disappeared 5 years ago.<br /> <br /> Talking about the 15 Essence 6 Dragon-Blooded in the Realm tells you nothing, and is innately misleading, in my opinion. Especially when it enters forum parlance with mentions of 'but then all the high-essence Dragon-Blooded in the Realm...' as if one were talking about DBZ power levels, rather than about the three extant who might be an excellent lover, an excellent poet, and another an excellent assassin who sucks at an open fight. There should be only as many high-essence beings as can have names and faces and stories, and <b>never</b> as amorphous numbers or descriptions.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","user":"Colapso","date":". 01-17-2015, 10:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T18:38:10-08:00","id":373957,"title":"","content":"Everytime a DB makes it to Elder status, they slip in the shower and die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T19:17:51-08:00","id":373966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/371833-the-number-of-elder-dragon-blooded?p=373957#post373957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everytime a DB makes it to Elder status, they slip in the shower and die.</div> </div> </div> </div> I thought a deva got its chakras","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1651-phalamir","name":"phalamir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T20:10:14-08:00","id":373986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/371833-the-number-of-elder-dragon-blooded?p=373943#post373943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Talking about the 15 Essence 6 Dragon-Blooded in the Realm tells you nothing, and is innately misleading, in my opinion. Especially when it enters forum parlance with mentions of 'but then all the high-essence Dragon-Blooded in the Realm...' as if one were talking about DBZ power levels, rather than about the three extant who might be an excellent lover, an excellent poet, and another an excellent assassin who sucks at an open fight. There should be only as many high-essence beings as can have names and faces and stories, and <b>never</b> as amorphous numbers or descriptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is not misleading if you don't jump to conclusions.<br /> <br /> Knowing that there is only a dozen or so Essence 6 Terrestrials means you treat them as unique treasures, rather than palette swap mook #32b with higher stats to use as part of the most recent Wyld Hunt. Thus each one should be treated like a character, fully flushed out and with their own styles &amp; ways of doing things. In fact if you consider the attrition rates in the combat oriented groups, it would be safe to say that a disproportionate number of the elders will the types who actively stay off the front lines.<br /> <br /> So yes you might have a grand master of all five Immaculate Dragon CMA styles, but he will be spending his time either in personal training or training others, rather than running around Creation. So unless the PCs are laying siege to the Cloister of Wisdom it is unlikely they would ever meet such a character regardless how many wyld hunts get called down on them.<br /> <br /> Now it is interesting to consider that in the case of Solars and potentially Abyssals, that one can produce very high numbers of Terrestrials with favorable Breeding scores and if given enough infrastructure, they can be trained right up to the edge of Essence 5 before they ever take the field. This in turn creates all sorts of political and social repercussions in the game if the ST plays it right, rather than freaking out about the munchkinish nature of it.<br /> <br /> According to the math I used there are only about 500 or so Essence 5 Terrestrials in the Realm and that is divided amongst five different directions with different character builds. Now imagine what happens on a social level if a solar shows up at Lookshy to sign an alliance treaty, but brings 500 (Essence 5 / Breeding 5) Terrestrials along as a body guard, each of which is fully combat trained and a competent sorcerer.<br /> <br /> Just by showing up with that kind of numbers, it will send shockwaves through the Realm and Lookshy. The military leaders will have to reconsider what they think they know about battlefield uses of Terrestrials, the priests who claim Terrestrial perfection will be confronted by the fact that Terrestrials who served a Solar lord are on average more powerful and of purer blood than those who follow the immaculate order, etc. etc.<br /> <br /> It can be amazing how many potent storyline hooks there are if one considers making power realistically rare and then letting the players flip things around.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T20:36:10-08:00","id":373999,"title":"","content":"How exactly are you producing 500 Essence 5 Breeding 5 Dragonblood? I'm sceptical that that is in any way practical in any sensible timeframe. Unless you're talking about doing it over 50 years or something (and obviously you need to kidnap two Breeding 5 Dragonblood first, and I assume then there's some plan involving Neomah?).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That gets even more strange when you consider Essence is not really a measure of <i>actual ability</i> in Exalted, and has never been: saying 'an Essence 6 character' accomplishes absolutely nothing. It is the array of Charms and Artifacts and connections that makes a character be actually relevant, and the amount of these entirely depends on how many named, important, earth-shaking characters you can have in mind. That <i>will vary between generations</i>. It absolutely has to! It's just how humans work! Those from generations that just happened to create several gifted figures will look upon a new generation with a certain contempt (even if some are gifted in different ways), and vice-versa, as older characters behold in a new generation so many children with talent such as he had never seen. </div> </div> </div>Exactly. A guy might sit on a mountain and meditate to raise his essence, but the other guy who spent his time practicing kung fu or sorcery or something, is actually more dangerous generally.<br /> <br /> Oh, and a couple of things to mention: for sorcerers and martial artists, Essence 6 just gives you 5 motes. It's not giving you access to any awesome charms at all. You could have learnt 5 more spells or kung fu charms instead.<br /> Actually, except for Wood Dragon stylists, that applies to Essence 5 as well (as the other styles only go up to Essence 4, and spells of course are all Essence 3).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 01-17-2015, 11:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T20:56:15-08:00","id":374032,"title":"","content":"I did not jump to conclusions, Thoth, as you just pointed out exactly what I spoke against.<br /> <br /> An 'Essence 5 Dragon-Blooded' - well, the actual equivalent to what you used a dehumanizing shorthand for - is a named, powerful hero. He is a gifted man, with his own legend, and his own reasons for reaching that high. He did not reach that high just because you put him through boot camp. He did not reach that high just because you gave him the right food. He is enlightened, driven, and unique. <br /> <br /> And you cannot have 500 vat-grown, factory-made, boot-camp trained of that guy. You cannot just 'create' that. Your efforts will leave you with... well, the equivalent of the Dynasty. With people who may all never raise past Essence 2, or if they do, and learn special techniques, will be for their own reasons. They are all heroes. They are all named. They are all their own people. And any who had the drive to raise himself that high will probably not be part of your group, unless he is a good friend... and I'm skeptical of anyone having 500 good friends.<br /> <br /> Such a hero would be an ally, a mentor, never a follower, and such heroes would never become a generic blob of numbers as you posited. I offer that is <i>bad for the game. </i>That is a terrible way of seeing it. It reduces the Dragon-Blooded, and it reduces the Exalted as a whole.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T22:18:40-08:00","id":374060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/371833-the-number-of-elder-dragon-blooded?p=373999#post373999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A guy might sit on a mountain and meditate to raise his essence, but the other guy who spent his time practicing kung fu or sorcery or something, is actually more dangerous generally.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does seem worth noting that the guy who went to sit on the mountaintop has made an investment in the future; he sacrifices the right-now payoff of having more kung fu or sorcery or whatnot with the comes-later payoff of more powerful Charms.<br /> <br /> Thinking about it, it actually seems likely to me that high-essence Dynasts will fall into three categories. The first are going to be Immaculates who dedicated themselves to pursuing that sort of life path as a way of enlightenment. The second are going to be people specifically detailed off by their House leadership to undergo that kind of training so that their House has access to the more powerful applications of essence that those with a deeper understanding of their own essence can access. The third are going to be people who have the kind of independence and drive to want to access that sort of path on their own. (And that's going to be a risk for them, as if I recall correctly raising your essence actually a process that can fail; only a PC is guaranteed to get a result from spending four months under that waterfall.)<br /> <br /> It may in fact be the case that the political leadership of the various Houses often (not always, but often) isn't particularly high-essence, as they don't have the time to spend trying to raise it because they're running their Houses, but they have access to people who are high-essence because they specifically made sure their House would have access to a guy who had access to custom-made Essence 5 Dragon-Blooded synergy charms <i>just in case</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/371833-the-number-of-elder-dragon-blooded?p=374032#post374032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An 'Essence 5 Dragon-Blooded' - well, the actual equivalent to what you used a dehumanizing shorthand for - is a named, powerful hero. He is a gifted man, with his own legend, and his own reasons for reaching that high. He did not reach that high just because you put him through boot camp. He did not reach that high just because you gave him the right food. He is enlightened, driven, and unique.<br /> <br /> And you cannot have 500 vat-grown, factory-made, boot-camp trained of that guy. You cannot just 'create' that. Your efforts will leave you with... well, the equivalent of the Dynasty. With people who may all never raise past Essence 2, or if they do, and learn special techniques, will be for their own reasons. They are all heroes. They are all named. They are all their own people. And any who had the drive to raise himself that high will probably not be part of your group, unless he is a good friend... and I'm skeptical of anyone having 500 good friends.<br /> <br /> Such a hero would be an ally, a mentor, never a follower, and such heroes would never become a generic blob of numbers as you posited. I offer that is <i>bad for the game. </i>That is a terrible way of seeing it. It reduces the Dragon-Blooded, and it reduces the Exalted as a whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would submit, Colapso, that would be bad for a Dragon-Blooded game.<br /> <br /> In a Solar game? I would have no trouble with Solar's boot-camping high-essence badass Dragon-Blooded, because one of the historical roles the Dragon-Blooded served were &quot;foot soldiers for the Solars.&quot; Those guys don't necessarily need to be protagonized. The PC's might of course choose to do so, but I would say it wouldn't hurt their game if they were pursuing an &quot;we mean for the Dragon-Blooded to resume their old places and are training them accordingly&quot; story arc where their company of Essence 4 or Essence 5 Dragon-Blooded badasses don't have much deeper names and faces than an equivalently sized company of Tiger-Warrior Trained mortals. Although it should, of course, be significantly harder to acquire.<br /> <br /> Not everyone who should be a legend is gonna be a legend. A lot of games just don't have room for that, and that's okay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T22:40:48-08:00","id":374068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/371833-the-number-of-elder-dragon-blooded?p=374032#post374032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you cannot have 500 vat-grown, factory-made, boot-camp trained of that guy. You cannot just 'create' that. Your efforts will leave you with... well, the equivalent of the Dynasty. With people who may all never raise past Essence 2, or if they do, and learn special techniques, will be for their own reasons. They are all heroes. They are all named. They are all their own people. And any who had the drive to raise himself that high will probably not be part of your group, unless he is a good friend... and I'm skeptical of anyone having 500 good friends.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually under 2nd edition you can which I have proven on multiple occasions.<br /> <br /> In the first method you have a solar who naturally will live for thousands of years, thus you can do this the long term way.<br /> <br /> In the second method you use a combination of rules and mechanics to mass produce Terrestrials and then train them. Using the scroll of heroes rules glitch that allows a single terrestrial regardless of gender to impregnate a near limitless amount of spirits and that the spirits can bring the baby to term in a matter of minutes you can literally mass produce children in any scale you want from dozens to thousands a day.<br /> <br /> If you combine the mechanics adjustments for a Terrestrial who has a higher essence than the spirit (preferably an elemental) and did the deed inside a Dragons Nest Manse, this basically ensures the terrestrial exaltation of the resulting offspring.<br /> <br /> Then you take the ton of offspring and ship them off to a trainer manse that has Wyld Revocation so that time inside the manse flows faster than the time in the rest of Creation. Thus in one to five years the entire batch exits the manse exalted, in their late teens, Essence 5, Sorcerers and knowing most if not all of the Terrestrial charm set. Thanks to Solar training charms and the AI based manse trainers, this is relatively easy to do.<br /> <br /> Does this dehumanize the Terrestrials in both character and concept, yes. But at the same time it is no different than walking into a random town that doesn't show up on the map, using social-fu charms to gain loyalty of the populace and then make them tiger warriors or rounding up thousands of Dragon Kings and civilizing them to be your minions. Or you could just get a factory cathedral and mass generating automatons or doing the same thing with a genesis laboratory and making biological minions.<br /> <br /> And yes I can cite the page references and rules as well as the exact manse designs to achieve this sort of mass production if you are curious.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/371833-the-number-of-elder-dragon-blooded?p=374032#post374032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Such a hero would be an ally, a mentor, never a follower, and such heroes would never become a generic blob of numbers as you posited. I offer that is <i>bad for the game. </i>That is a terrible way of seeing it. It reduces the Dragon-Blooded, and it reduces the Exalted as a whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue that this concept is the core of Exalted.<br /> <br /> Because you have a divine patron who picks a shmuck out of the masses, empowers them and then sends them off to fight and probably die to advance that Patrons agenda for Creation. That fits the Unconquered Sun, Luna, The Five Maidens, The Deathlords, the Yozis, Autochthon and to a certain extent the Elemental Dragons.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T23:18:00-08:00","id":374082,"title":"","content":"Thoth, bearing in mind that 2nd edition bungled that in general, you're mention using rules from the Scroll of Heroes, which is considered a mistake in GENERAL.<br /> <br /> Just because something was published doesn't mean it is a good idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/371833-the-number-of-elder-dragon-blooded?p=374068#post374068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would argue that this concept is the core of Exalted.<br /> <br /> Because you have a divine patron who picks a shmuck out of the masses, empowers them and then sends them off to fight and probably die to advance that Patrons agenda for Creation. That fits the Unconquered Sun, Luna, The Five Maidens, The Deathlords, the Yozis, Autochthon and to a certain extent the Elemental Dragons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. These people are given the potential to be heroes. To carve their own legends.<br /> <br /> Becoming a number in a generic blob is the very opposite of the core concept of Exalted.<br /> <br /> Exalted are never extras, and each conflict in the setting shows well that they cannot be treated in these generic terms - to create 500 DBs, of any power, like that is to engineer your very own, personal Usurpation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T01:23:58-08:00","id":374120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/371833-the-number-of-elder-dragon-blooded?p=374082#post374082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because something was published doesn't mean it is a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't want to get me started on how many things are a bad idea in exalted. It is entirely possible to write a supplement sized book just going over all the design flaws and the ways it caters only to certain player types. Hell the way Martial Arts was designed and implemented in Exalted is about on par with a virgin writing a fan fiction sex scene.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/371833-the-number-of-elder-dragon-blooded?p=374082#post374082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Becoming a number in a generic blob is the very opposite of the core concept of Exalted.<br /> <br /> Exalted are never extras, and each conflict in the setting shows well that they cannot be treated in these generic terms - to create 500 DBs, of any power, like that is to engineer your very own, personal Usurpation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find the notion of being the badass anime character trope to be boring and pointless. The wandering hero shtick was played out for me by the 1990s, then again so was playing the villain. Exalted is supposed to be about playing an RPG on a truly epic scale. But what exactly is epic in this case?<br /> <br /> It isn't fighting a hundred guys by yourself, it isn't making a poem that makes the gods themselves weep, it isn't creating a new sorcery spell and it isn't recreating a character clone from an anime you saw one time.<br /> <br /> I ask people what their end game would look like for a given storyline or character. The responses I get are generally things like &quot;I beat up the realm&quot; or &quot;recreate the deliberative&quot;. But they rarely if ever get that far.<br /> <br /> In my sort of games, the fall of the Realm is a beginning to middle game sort of storyline. Forget recreating the Deliberative, I am thinking making something new, something different. I don't want to push the world map from its core book scale back to the Dreams of the First Age scale, I want to carve out a map the size of that one fan made one that shows the blessed isle as barely an inch across compared to the rest of Creation.<br /> <br /> But here is the thing, after a certain point, things like Terrestrials and Dragon Kings become mundane NPC mooks. So when I talk about how to deal with breeding an army of Terrestrials it is from the perspective of those sorts of later plans where just being exalted doesn't really account for much.<br /> <br /> Consider for a moment what sort of threats you would have to design to threaten a Creation where every major city is an alchemical Metropolis, each one boasting a standing Terrestrial Legions of 50,0000 Dragon-Blooded and another 200,000 Tiger Warriors. Consider a Creation so huge that the Terrestrials and Alchemicals have an equal say to the regular celestials just due to numbers. Consider a Creation where some of my most insane Manse designs are everyday infrastructure and in some cases the only way to manage a Creation of that size. Because that is the sort of game the Exalted system is supposed to let you play.<br /> <br /> Consider that sort of game setting for a moment, let it simmer in your mind. Now hop on the forums and listen to people talk about if it is toxic to the setting or not to allow some one to breed a couple hundred Terrestrials. Because to me, complaining about that just feels like such a lack of imagination and drive.<br /> <br /> A person can go to any other game setting and play a character that accomplishes nothing of note, but in Exalted your starting character is essentially where most other games force character retirement. By that same concept the end game designs should be similarly out of this world. But instead all I hear about is the same levels of dreck I heard about back in my days playing AD&amp;D. It is disappointing to say the least.<br /> <br /> I will step off my soap box now....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T02:38:48-08:00","id":374139,"title":"","content":"You know, thinking about it, Thoth's idea of mass-producing DBs is excellent.<br /> Why? Because it's the start of a ton of teen superhero/sci-fi stories.<br /> You (the PCs) are a group of teenagers raised in an institution by an evil scientist to be his footsoldiers. He uses propaganda to brainwash you. But then, you find out something or other, and start to question things. One of your friends gets killed for knowing too much/being too rebellious. Plus, your teenagers and want to control your own lives.<br /> So you break out.<br /> Now, you're a group of unlikely teenage heroes who fight monsters in between your relationship drama, while the overall arch is you trying to take down the evil scientist who created you, and when you meet him you have an argument about how you own your own bodies, and aren't just his slaves, that you should be allowed to make your own choices, etc. Also, he sends his goons after you, but he foolishly gave you awesome powers so you normally beat them.<br /> Presumably the meaning of the story is something about strict parenthood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T04:38:32-08:00","id":374169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/371833-the-number-of-elder-dragon-blooded?p=374120#post374120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consider for a moment what sort of threats you would have to design to threaten a Creation where every major city is an alchemical Metropolis, each one boasting a standing Terrestrial Legions of 50,0000 Dragon-Blooded and another 200,000 Tiger Warriors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not give us some ideas? This seems to be your preferred level of play rather than the outright victory most groups would consider it as. What challenges do empires like that face?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T06:06:41-08:00","id":374241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/371833-the-number-of-elder-dragon-blooded?p=374169#post374169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not give us some ideas? This seems to be your preferred level of play rather than the outright victory most groups would consider it as. What challenges do empires like that face?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well first off as you expand the size of Creation, you end up expanding the size of the Underworld. So even if you have created a strong society and pushed the Deathlords back into the Underworld and hunted down practically every shadowland, the Underworld and its denizens remain. Since you have expanded the Underworld so greatly, this means the Deathlords and the Neverborn will be more entrenched and powerful than ever before.<br /> <br /> Imagine the sort of scenario you could face if all the deathlords started actually working together in a unified fashion with no pretense of hiding what they are capable of. The last time something even close to that happened resulted in the Great Contagion.<br /> <br /> Eventually you will want to take the fight to the Underworld itself rather than just containing incursions. But this means changing tactics because all the essence works differently there than it does in Creation. This means your Terrestrial troops and even some of the Celestials are limited in power duration. Of course even if you some how manage to defeat the deathlords and put more functional bindings on the Neverborn, the only way to ensure Underworld compliance is to colonize it. This in turn means a whole new breeding program to create strains of Death-Tainted Dragon-Blooded to permanently live in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> The threats from the Yozis are kind of a permanent thing so you have a continuous threat of Akuma and Infernal attacks. Though I could easily see using Malfeas as a training grounds for fun and profit.<br /> <br /> But for truly huge scale stuff, consider the possibilities of Creations made by rogue Primordials deep in the Wyld. We have the example of the one the Unconquered Sun destroyed, but it wasn't entirely wiped out, so it could have been rebuilt. There could now be dozens of such Creations all poised to attack.<br /> <br /> Then there is the side story of that Terrestrial in the late First Age that was given a dream to take almost an entire gens into the deep wyld. If they survived to this day, how many of them could there be? They could easily return to creation not unlike the clans from the MechWarrior lore that returned to the core system to reassert their dominance with thousands of years of weapons tech development. Perhaps to get around the limitations of their Terrestrial natures, they started upgrading themselves like the borg or warhammer 40k tech priests to gain access to something that approximates celestial crafting charms.<br /> <br /> Of course there is always the Well of Udr, which if it truly is a gateway of sorts to alternate realties and other worlds, well then you could just as easily add access to the Gunstar Autochonia setting for cross over events and having to deal with a fighting force of Primordials that is actually stronger than anything previously faced. But this starts getting into DC Comics levels of alternate earths with your one reality slowly consuming and adjusting the rest.<br /> <br /> Then there is the fact that &quot;temporal weapons&quot; were used in the Primordial War, so eventually either by being reengineered or by finding a remaining one, you can get into a nasty form of Time War which can draw on Dr. Who levels of messing around with things. Then cross that with the Well of Udr and things get......complicated.<br /> <br /> But strangely enough when you take a step back from it all, yeah a lot of this is only possible because you have some Celestial Exalts setting things up and planning this out, but in truth it is almost impossible to pull off without the unlimited Terrestrials and potentially the Alchemicals.<br /> <br /> Of course if you convert some of the Infernals into new Primordials, well then things really become interesting. Because then you start running two games back to back, where one game you are playing the Exalt crew that built this grand end game scenario, then the second game is having the players using different characters trying to bring it down. Their knowledge of the setting and situations makes them their own worst enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T09:29:40-08:00","id":374297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/371833-the-number-of-elder-dragon-blooded?p=373934#post373934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Without that concept, though, doesn't the whole breeding thing break down? If there was never a time when the Dragon-Blooded existed in a sort of idealized form, where they always bred true because they only bred with each other, then the whole bloodline thing breaks down.</div> </div> </div> </div>No it doesn't, as evidenced by the fact that it's a perfectly serviceable portrayal of the best bred families of the contemporary Realm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Second Age is chronically short of Dragon-Blooded and always has been.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it was chronically short just after the Contagion, but by the timeline of games they have about as many as they need and not so many that they're likely to tear the world apart. The Realm manufactures incentives to have many Exalted children, but it also creates obstacles against having them indiscriminately.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's certainly possible to establish that context, but why would you want to?</div> </div> </div> </div>To create a sense of meaningful difference between an Age of Sorrows and one of prosperity. Like, the social implications of food shortages create some truly fascinating stories, and yet I still wouldn't find a portrayal of the First Age in which they were much of a problem to be credible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You always want more Exalts, because that translates into more political and military power</div> </div> </div> </div>More chaos, more infighting...<br /> <br /> Incidentally, there's a bit in the Second Edition core's description of the Realm (a summary of that society which I've always really liked) which frames the relationship between Dynasts in a way I think is good, where the elders manage things on the Blessed Isle (particularly the distribution of stipends) and rely on the younger ones to go around in pull in money and power. It gives me a picture of a more direct, personal, intimate form of power hierarchies in Dragon Blooded families, where the juniors whom you direct in political games are more singular and specific than just sublimating into enormous masses of pawns. Between that and some of the figures given for numbers and frequency of children, I'd say the usual pattern is of an established Terrestrial couple having a single child who grows into their intermediary to the wider world until they become established enough to start their own families, and then you have another single child and start over.<br /> <br /> Maybe also an image where you have several children within a few years of each other, but only expect one of them to Exalt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, I've always gotten the impression that the Shogunate was as well, because the Shogunate was trying to hold together a global hegemony built on Solar infrastructure with only Dragon-Blooded, and the result of that was lots of Dragon-Blooded dying as they tried to hold back the Wyld and there were never enough Sorcerer-Technicians to go around and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whereabouts? It doesn't seem very evident in the Aspect books; rather the opposite, really, if Aspect Book: Air is anything to go by.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercushio</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">you probably had Twilight's deciding things like &quot;no, you know what? This whole 'Exaltation through the blood' thing is interesting to me. How pure a Dragon-Blood can I develop?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>And a lot of people who were Exalted who could tell such people where to stick it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T14:46:45-08:00","id":374463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/371833-the-number-of-elder-dragon-blooded?p=374241#post374241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*snip*</div> </div> </div> </div> Nothing new there. I was really hoping for something less &quot;five year plan&quot; and more actual gaming experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T20:51:38-08:00","id":374822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In fact, I've always gotten the impression that the Shogunate was as well, because the Shogunate was trying to hold together a global hegemony built on Solar infrastructure with only Dragon-Blooded, and the result of that was lots of Dragon-Blooded dying as they tried to hold back the Wyld and there were never enough Sorcerer-Technicians to go around and the like. </div> </div> </div> Whereabouts? It doesn't seem very evident in the Aspect books; rather the opposite, really, if Aspect Book: Air is anything to go by. </div> </div> </div>From the (extremely small amounts of) information on the Shogunate, the impression I got is not that there wasn't enough sorcerer-engineers per-se, but rather that the sorcerer-engineers simply weren't good enough. They needed to be able to cast Celestial and Solar sorcery, to use Solar medicine charms, to use Wyld-Shaping, and they couldn't, at all. They tried to make up for it with slave labour and masses of sorcerer-engineers (which is why they trained sorcerers as government officials), but no amount would ever be enough to maintain what they were trying to do.<br /> At the same time, the mass of Dragonblooded families with their armies of first-age weapons were always fighting over who should be Shogun. It was after all, a feudal system, and feudal systems tend to be extremely violent.<br /> If there were less Dragonblood, there probably would be less civil war (but of course, it would also be harder to maintain the infrastructure and defend against the Fae, and so on... but the main problem was the constant civil wars. Until the Contagion of course.).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T04:28:59-08:00","id":375132,"title":"","content":"The way the Second Edition core lines up the whole thing is actually pretty nifty, now that I give it more consideration. The idea that newly graduated Dynasts go off to live with other relatives provides the skeleton for how the Great Houses are a coordination of enormous extended families, cross pollinating individual households rather than letting them just build up inside of themselves, while still existing under the direction of ancestors of the next step up (meaning that, while your adult children go off to be under the more direct authority of your siblings or cousins rather than yourself, they still fall under the umbrella of your grandparents and great-grandparents).<br /> <br /> It also provides a context for why there are diminishing returns for having too many young Dragon Blooded under one roof, and it's about the same as when they're still children; the expense. It just changes from the expense of educating them to the expense of rewarding them for their household services (which is also partly the expense of educating your own children <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />).<br /> <br /> It's a good way to emphasize that Dragon Blooded are never pawns, they're simply players who operate in different arenas of the game. After you graduate (and have your first wild vacation in the Threshold), you join another household of your family (or possibly your father's family), and bring the values of being young, vigorous, lacking social establishment and a steady job or family, the values of being somebody who can be sent out to acquire assets or further interests for them while they remain home and oversee their own responsibilities, and in return you get expensive gifts, introductions and commendations, being delegated portions of your host's property. You're not a pawn, you're an agent, and one worth overseeing directly (and expensive enough to be about the limit of what they can manage).<br /> <br /> Indeed, that kind of cross-pollinated mentor system probably also helps maintain the conservatism of Dynast society, because you get to bring that young, vigorous, possibly even idealistic new demigod under the wings of the establishment, where they can be moulded into upholding the status quo and thus eventually assume their own place as somebody with a job that maintains the Realm and a marriage that ensures the future of the Dynasty. After all, the things that make junior Dynasts so valuable to their seniors are also the exact kinds of things that can make them terribly dangerous; youthful energy that could be directed against you, lack of social standing to undermine or attack, no established assets or responsibilities to target or take away. No, better to manage each one carefully, make them care about those things so that they'll work for you to be given them, and thereafter they're just like you and little threat to the system. It's for their own good anyway; surely that model for Dynast society and life cycle is the superior way in which to live, since it's the one you grew up in yourself.<br /> <br /> If you had large numbers of young people who were all gathered at once in non-descript masses in which you couldn't really take a direct hand in managing them, well, they might start consulting one another on how to do things, might start getting <i>ideas</i>, and nobody wants that. Something the size of a Sworn Brotherhood is fine, but the very idea of a Dragon Blooded youth movement? I can imagine the Scarlet Empress grew up with horror stories of places in the Shogunate that went all Les Miserables, and was eager to shape her Dynasty to avoid it.<br /> <br /> Hence scenarios in which having the largest number of Dragon Blooded, especially young adult ones, isn't actually very optimal at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}